<title>UK: EIB sets $500 mln 10-year bond to be priced +18 bp.</title>
<headline>EIB sets $500 mln 10-year bond to be priced +18 bp.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Goldman Sachs and SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT    $500 MLN	COUPON     **	  MATURITY    23.APR.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    23.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.0 PCT   REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+18 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.325     SELL CONC  1.675     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.25 PCT FEB 2007 U.S. TREASURY  NOTES	** TO BE PRICED</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
